    Text = "<Title:[SSR Items]>\nIn the [Realms Research] Standard Character Awakening, the base probability for SSR items is 3.03%, with overall probability (including guarantees) of 5.02%. All SSR items are Awakeners, with a guaranteed SSR Awakener after maximum 30 Awakenings.\nThe following limited Awakener types from the Faded Legacy have been added to the \"Realms Research\" standard awakening and share a total of 0.5% of the overall SSR Awakener rate in their respective realms, but these limited Awakener types cannot be obtained through the \"Protoparadise\".\n○ [<SummonOrange:Chaos>] Realm: \"Lily\", \"24\", \"Ryker\", \"Hameln\", \"Tawil\"\n○ [<SummonBlue:Aequor>] Realm: \"Tulu\", \"Murphy\", \"Miryam\"\n○ [<SummonRed:Caro>] Realm: \"Sorel\", \"Salvador\", \"Thais\", \"Helot: Catena\"\n○ [<SummonPurple:Ultra>] Realm: \"Daffodil\", \"Wanda\", \"Horla\" \n\n<Title:[\"SR Items\"]>\nIn the [Realms Research] Standard Character Awakening, the base probability of obtaining an SR item is 15.85%, and the overall probability (including guarantees) is 25.02%. All SR items in this awakening are Wheel of Destiny. \nA maximum of 5 awakenings will definitely guarantee obtaining SR or higher items, with a 96.97% probability of obtaining an SR item through the pity system and a 3.03% probability of obtaining an SSR item. \n\n<Title:[\"Special Notes\"]>\nWhen obtaining an SR Wheel of Destiny through awakening, 5 Radix Sediments will also be obtained as by-products; when obtaining an R Wheel of Destiny, 1 Radix Sediment will be obtained as a by-product. \nRegardless of the method used (including but not limited to awakening, store exchange, system gifts, etc.), for the 2nd to 16th times obtaining the same SSR Awakener, each time will convert to 1 corresponding Awakener Shard and 50 Radix Sediments; from the 17th time onwards, it will convert to 1 Refined Gnosis Fragment, 3 Gnosis Fragments, and 150 Radix Sediments, while limited SSR Awakener types will convert to 2 Refined Gnosis Fragments, 6 Gnosis Fragments, and 250 Radix Sediments. However, obtaining an Awakener or excess Awakener Shards through any selected method (including Protoparadise, Rebirth Core, Prototype Horizon) will not convert into Radix Sediments. \nThis awakening belongs to [Standard Character Awakening], and the pity awakening count will be accumulated separately, independent of the pity counts of other awakening types. \n\n"
  },
